    "Reason : 1 - The developer has provided insufficient information to enable the authority to establish whether the proposed development complies with the conditions, limitations or restrictions specified in Class J applicable to the development in question. The Local Planning Authority is unable to assess the design or external appearance of the development, and the impact of glare on occupiers of neighbouring land in the absence of proposed elevations and glint and glare details.\r\nThe proposal is therefore contrary to Condition J.4 of Schedule 2 Part 14 Class J of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).\r\n"
